    "result_text": "**All 3 invariants proved safe.** Summary:\n\nAll three canonical economic invariants for the vault + accrual/rebase contract were machine-checked and proved safe by solc's SMTChecker (CHC engine with z3):\n\n1. **fees_monotonic** (3/3 VCs) — proved via pre-state snapshot: `accumulatedFees` only increases in `accrual` (via `+= fee`) and is untouched in `deposit`/`withdraw`, so it is non-decreasing across every state transition.\n2. **accrual_on_balance_change** (2/2 VCs) — proved via ghost flag `_accrualApplied` reset at function entry and set by `_applyAccrual()`: every function that modifies a user's balance calls the accrual helper first, so balance change implies accrual was applied.\n3. **solvency_with_accrual** (3/3 VCs) — proved as an inductive invariant with `require(totalAssets >= totalShares)` as precondition: deposit adds equally to both, withdraw subtracts equally from both (1:1 redemption), and accrual only increases `totalAssets`, preserving the solvency gap.\n\nAll proofs were vacuity-checked by mutating asserts to `assert(false)` and confirming the solver produced counterexamples (paths are reachable). No invariant was left unproved.",
